# Handoff — 2026-08-06: cli-consumer-ux SHIPPED (commit 1a6bfca)

## What was built

Pack `cli-consumer-ux` — UX revisit of `agentide-cli-consumer` (row 28 of the
backlog). Fixes two operator-blocking issues from the 2026-08-06 e2e test:

* **D-79 (Critical):** `agentide invoke <business-cap>` now auto-mints a
  session via `session.create`+invoke+`session.destroy` when `--session`
  is omitted. Supplied `--session` is reused (no destroy). Driven by
  `packages/agentide/src/session-mint.ts` (`withAutoSession`).
* **D-80 (High):** `--url` with no port defaults to `7300` (websocket
  adapter / consumer door). Pointing at the SDK door `7350` emits a
  clear `error: --url points to the SDK door (port 7350); the CLI
  consumer needs the websocket adapter (port 7300).` and exits 2 —
  detected by a 3s auth-handshake timeout in the WS client
  (`WsDoorMismatchError`). Driven by
  `packages/agentide/src/url-default.ts` (`applyPortDefault`) and
  `packages/adapter-websocket/src/client.ts` (`authTimeoutMs`).
* **Q3 (watch lifecycle):** `agentide watch` auto-mints, keeps the
  session alive for the watch lifetime, destroys on clean exit.
  Driven by `runWatch` in `packages/agentide/src/consumer.ts`.

## What the next session should do

The pack is SHIPPED. The user is in good shape. The next natural pack
is a **CLI quality-of-life** that closes the still-open drifts:

* D-78 (Medium) — `agentide init --data-dir <fresh>` fails with raw
  ENOENT. Should mkdir or print the same hint `start` does.
* D-81 (Medium) — `agentide status` (no --data-dir) defaults to
  cwd-relative `./.agentide/data`. Fails when start was elsewhere.
  Pid file should track data-dir.
* D-83 (Low) — `agentide stop` exit codes inconsistent (0 vs 1) for
  same "nothing running" state.
* D-84 (Low) — `client grant` flag mismatch (CLI expects
  --tenant/--name, not --client-id/--scope); no per-subcommand help.

Plus the cli-consumer-ux accepted drifts:

* D-85 (Low) — PRD Scenario 5 wording fixed; mark resolved.
* D-86 (Low) — IPv6 host test added in this session; mark resolved.
* D-87 (Low) — Phase 5 always-destroy warning; acceptable, no action.
* D-88 (Low) — Scenario 2 batch sim section added; mark resolved.
* D-89 (Low) — consumer.ts 407 lines, over AGENTS.md rule 9 cap of 350.
  Future pack should extract runWatch/runWatchInner to watch.ts.

